{
  "_comment": [
    "The diners the racers go to, by level (see docs/modding.md, \"diners\"). Each takes the cars from powerFrom",
    "horsepower up to the next diner's floor: a racer is a regular of the diner their car's dyno figure puts them in (a",
    "boss of the top one), and the regulars of a diner above the player's car won't race them, though every diner is open",
    "to go and look. The first diner (from 0) is where everybody starts out. street: the street the diner stands on (a",
    "street with a diner.json); one with no such street yet is seen on the first diner's street. stakes: how many times",
    "the house limits the cash bets go for there. name, about, region: text keys (left out: diner.name.<id>,",
    "diner.about.<id>, diner.region.<id>). mapX, mapY: where it is on the diners' map, fractions of the whole picture",
    "as the dealers' are (dealers/dealers.json says how they are measured); left out, the diner is not on the map.",
    "look: what the diner wears on its street: layout, laid over the street's layout (street.json; docs/modding.md,",
    "streets' layout): its own spots (its roof board, its billboard, what stands in its lot: pieces of the street kit),",
    "its own versions of the street's named slots (its palms, its trees, its shops) and drop (the street's slots it has none of), and",
    "weights (how much more often a piece of a tag is picked: the Hi-Way's trucks and brick, Surfside's beach cars, the",
    "Starlite's big iron), so each save lays out a street of each diner's own; approach: its own way in, back out and",
    "out and where the driver looks (as diner.json's), to a curb across the street from it; its own sun, lights (a light of the day",
    "keeps the street's lamps, recoloured by lampColor, and adds its lamps; positions are the street's, see street.json)",
    "and glow (by material, over the street's). show: a mod's street model's look groups shown (nodes named LOOK_<GROUP>",
    "...), the base game's has none. The four share Main Street's stage until each has a street of its own; a curb of",
    "Main Street with no diner to go by wears the first diner's look."
  ],
